That's not you, that's Google Groups' software maintainers
being stupid and stubborn.

Stupid, because (since they mix emailing and posting in the
same interface) they quote lines beginning with "From " or
"from " as if the posting were email.

Stubborn, because I've reported this bug to them more than
half a dozen times over the course of more than a year.

The end result in your case is that, flowing through the
software, the now quoted ">From " hit another of their
bugs, that omits whitespace between quoted paragraphs,
decided your first line was part of the previous paragraph
and moved it up, then noticed that your next line was _not_
quoted, and moved it down to leave some whitespace.

That created the mess you see; your input was probably
just fine.

Grrrr.

xanthian.

